{{!< default}}

{{!-- The Feed Surface: every post, newest first, paginated — in whichever layout the
publication picked.

The layout picker is the pattern home.hbs documents: the setting is read here and handed to
feed/surface.hbs as `layout`, which holds the one {{#match}}, and no partial below reads @custom.

No query here. Unlike the homepage, this Surface IS its own query: `posts` is the page's slice of
the collection or channel that owns this URL, and `pagination` is the shape of the rest of it.
That is also why the theme cannot decide how many rows a page holds — Ghost resolves the limit in
the routing layer, from `posts_per_page` in this theme's package.json or from `limit:` on the
route in the publication's routes.yaml, both of which are settled long before a template runs.

This template also serves page 2 onwards of a `/` collection: with the layout in
docs/routes.example.yaml the cover owns `/` and this Surface owns `/archive/`, but a publication
that leaves `/` as its posts collection gets the cover on page 1 and this Surface on every page
after it. Both are correct, and neither needs a branch here. --}}

{{> "chrome/header"}}

<main
	id="main"
	class="grow"
	data-surface="feed"
	data-layout="{{#match @custom.feed_layout "Grid"}}Grid{{else}}List{{/match}}">

	{{> "feed/surface" layout=@custom.feed_layout}}

</main>

{{> "chrome/footer"}}
